# ============================================================================
# Agent repository .gitignore — SuperHermes normalised standard.
#
# MODEL: default-deny. The repo re-includes the agent's durable identity and its
# open `vault/` workspace (ENTIRE vault tracked — Chief decision 2026-08-06). Everything else stays out by construction.
# Known credential payloads and generated machine state remain excluded by the
# final rules; secret scanning is required before commits because the Brain is
# intentionally open to normal working files.
#
# This file is NORMALISED across the fleet (every agent follows this standard)
# but NOT CENTRALISED — each agent keeps its own copy at its root. Slug below is
# the only per-agent value. Regenerate from SuperHermes/templates/gitignore.tmpl.
#   agent slug: __AGENT_SLUG__
# ============================================================================

# ── 0. Deny everything by default ───────────────────────────────────────────
*

# ── 1. Repo control + top-level operating docs ──────────────────────────────
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/docs/
!/docs/**
!/memory/
!/memory/**
!/ops/
!/ops/**
!/workspace-index/
!/workspace-index/**

# ── 1a. Canonical agent Brain — open private workspace ───────────────────────
# `vault/` is the open workspace root; `vault/brain/` remains the canonical Brain. The agent owns its contents
# and may organise any useful files beneath it; suggested folders are guidance,
# not gates. Final Brain-specific rules below reopen ordinary asset types while
# keeping credential payloads and generated machine state out of Git history.
!/vault/

# ── 2. The Hermes profile — identity, skills, and plugins ────────────────────
# Re-include each ancestor directory so git can descend, then the specific
# durable artifacts within. (Default-deny means every parent must be re-opened.)
!/.hermes/
!/.hermes/SOUL.md
!/.hermes/sandbox/
!/.hermes/sandbox/__AGENT_SLUG__.sb
!/.hermes/profiles/
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/config.yaml
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/repos.yaml
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/SOUL.md
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/memories/
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/memories/*.md
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/cron/
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/cron/jobs.definition.json
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/scripts/
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/scripts/**
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/skills/
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/skills/**
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/plugins/
!/.hermes/profiles/__AGENT_SLUG__/plugins/**

# ── 3. Belt-and-suspenders: never track these even inside allowed trees ──────
# (Last-match-wins: these come AFTER the allow-list so they always win.)
# Secrets / credentials
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/auth.json
**/*google_token*
**/*token*
**/*credential*
**/*secret*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.kdbx
**/*.age
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/*.git-credentials

# Profile skills/plugins are intentional source. Re-open them after broad
# name-based credential denials (e.g. **/*token*) so directories like
# token_monitor / token-audit remain trackable. Runtime secret filenames below
# still win afterward.
!/.hermes/profiles/*/skills/
!/.hermes/profiles/*/skills/**
!/.hermes/profiles/*/plugins/
!/.hermes/profiles/*/plugins/**
# Keep secret payloads out even inside skills/plugins trees
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/auth.json
**/*secret*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.kdbx
**/*.age
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/*.git-credentials
**/.hub/
**/.archive/
**/.usage.json*
**/.usage.json.lock
# Profile skill hygiene
**/skills_disabled/
**/skills/**/templates/**/*.pdf
**/.bundled_manifest
**/.curator_state
**/.curator_backups/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo

# Runtime state / locks / sessions / logs
**/logs/
**/sessions/
**/cron/output/
**/*.lock
**/*.pid
**/*.log
**/*.jsonl
**/gateway_state.json
**/processes.json
**/.usage.json*
**/.usage.json.lock
**/.curator_state
**/.curator_backups/
**/.hub/
**/.archive/
# Memory/model binary stores — human-useful Brain assets are allowed, never generated indexes
**/*.pglite
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*.wal
**/*.shm
**/localmem_chroma/
**/chroma*/
**/*.gguf
**/*.safetensors
**/*.pt
**/*.pth
**/*.onnx
**/*.bin
# Caches / build / deps
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/vendor/
# Generated media / archives
**/*.png
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.gif
**/*.webp
**/*.mp4
**/*.mov
**/*.ogg
**/*.mp3
**/*.wav
**/*.pdf
**/*.zip
**/*.tar
**/*.tar.gz
**/.DS_Store
*.bak*

# ── 4. Big trees that never belong in the identity repo (clarity; already
#       covered by default-deny since they were never re-included) ───────────
# /.hermes/backups/  database dumps
# /.home/ /.cache/ /.npm/ /.local/ /.ollama/ /tmp/   isolated runtime + caches
# /vault/            ENTIRE vault is tracked (open workspace) — see section 5
# /workspace/        working area + third-party clones — never the agent identity

# ── 5. Open vault workspace — normal files are first-class ──────────────────
# This comes last so ordinary Brain assets (images, PDFs, audio, canvases, JSON,
# spreadsheets, archives, etc.) override the repository-wide generated-media
# ignores above. These rules govern Git history only; they never limit what an
# agent may create or use locally.
!/vault/
!/vault/**

# Credentials and generated machine state belong outside the vault and
# remain out of source control even if accidentally written beneath this root.
/vault/**/.env
/vault/**/.env.*
/vault/**/auth.json
/vault/**/*google_token*.json
/vault/**/*credential*.json
/vault/**/*secret*.json
/vault/**/*token*.json
/vault/**/.secrets/
/vault/**/secrets/
/vault/**/.credentials/
/vault/**/credentials/
/vault/**/*.pem
/vault/**/*.key
/vault/**/*.p12
/vault/**/*.pfx
/vault/**/*.kdbx
/vault/**/*.age
/vault/**/id_rsa*
/vault/**/id_ed25519*
/vault/**/.git-credentials
/vault/**/.runtime/
/vault/**/runtime/
/vault/**/.gbrain/
/vault/**/gbrain-data/
/vault/**/.cache/
/vault/**/.herenow/
/vault/**/node_modules/
/vault/**/.venv/
/vault/**/__pycache__/
/vault/**/*.pglite
/vault/**/*.sqlite
/vault/**/*.sqlite3
/vault/**/*.db
/vault/**/*.db-*
/vault/**/*.wal
/vault/**/*.shm
/vault/**/*.lock
/vault/**/*.pid
/vault/**/.DS_Store
/vault/**/*.bak*

# Large scraped vendor dumps that trip secret scanners with example tokens
**/unsloth/references/llms-full.md
**/unsloth/references/llms-txt.md
